  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Hawaii has received $2.4B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Contract activity in Hawaii includes 21,391 awards with an average award size of $111K. Obligations fell 56.9% year over year. Yearly totals show a peak in FY24 at $6.7B, followed by $5.5B in FY25 and $2.4B in FY26. Construction and engineering dominate current-year spending. Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction accounted for $602M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounted for $458M. The Department of Defense remains the largest buyer, obligating $1.8B in FY2026 to date. Large construction and services contractors lead the vendor list. DRAGADOS/HAWAIIAN DREDGING/ORION JV received $354M and NAN INC received $272M. This snapshot covers partial fiscal-year totals and shows a sharp decline from last year alongside concentrated activity in a few industries, agencies, and vendors.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations fall 56.9% year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 56.9% year over year. Fiscal-year totals show FY24 at $6.7B and FY25 at $5.5B, then FY26 at $2.4B. Large swings in annual obligations suggest year-to-year variation in major projects and contract timing. Hawaii’s current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors concentrate federal spending in Hawaii?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.8B in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $297M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $115M. DRAGADOS/HAWAIIAN DREDGING/ORION JV received $354M and NAN INC received $272M. Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction accounted for $602M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounted for $458M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Hawaii?",
      "a": "Hawaii received $2.4B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 21,391 awards with an average award size of $111K. Obligations fell 56.9% year over year, and annual totals show FY24 at $6.7B, FY25 at $5.5B, and FY26 at $2.4B."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Hawaii?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.8B in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $297M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $115M. Other top agencies include the Department of Veterans Affairs with $45.4M and the Department of the Interior with $36M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Hawaii?",
      "a": "DRAGADOS/HAWAIIAN DREDGING/ORION JV is the largest federal contractor in Hawaii, receiving $354M in FY2026 to date. NAN INC received $272M and CONTI FEDERAL SERVICES, LLC received $97.3M. Other leading vendors include HENSEL PHELPS CONSTRUCTION CO with $87.2M and LEIDOS, INC. with $83.9M."
